able[p_state][c]\n                        //       // next_last_c = c\n                        //       // next_addr = ((next_S_idx * 6) + next_p) * 6 + next_last_c\n                        //       // Read existing data at next_addr\n                        //       // Compute new data\n                        //       // Write back\n                        //       \n                        //       // This requires reading existing data from RAM.\n                        //       // We are iterating S_idx 0..MAX-1.\n                        //       // We read from RAM at `next_addr`.\n                        //       // We write to RAM at `next_addr`.\n                        //       // Since `next_S_idx` > `S_idx`, we are writing to a state\n                        //       // that we haven't processed as a source yet.\n                        //       // This is fine.\n                        //       \n                        //   We need to handle p_state and last_c iteration.\n                        //   We have 3 nested loops: S_idx, p_state, last_c.\n                        //   \n                        //   Loop structure:\n                        //   for S_idx 0..MAX-1:\n                        //     decode used_counts\n                        //     for p_state 0..pattern_len:\n                        //       for last_c 0..5:\n                        //         Read curr_data = RAM[ ((S_idx*6)+p_state)*6 + last_c ]\n                        //         If curr_data.count > 0:\n                        //           for color c 0..n-1:\n                        //             if valid(c):\n                        //               update RAM[ ((next_S_idx*6)+next_p)*6 + c ]\n                        //             end\n                        //           end\n                        //         end\n                        //       end\n                        //     end\n                        //   end\n                        //   \n                   